From 4030ef8d7964b0ebaaea3403f3dc6d7abdd58f4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:14:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 122/210] media: amlogic: amvdec: add HEVC decoding

Decode HEVC slice requests with synthesized headers, short-term reference
sets and timestamp-resolved DPB entries. Validate coded geometry, tiles
and motion-vector extents before programming the decoder. Refuse long-term
prediction and single-column multi-row pictures.

Add shared HEVC framebuffer compression, MMU maps and capture backing.
Support Main and Main10 at 3840x2160 on every compatible. GX uses
contiguous compressed references and double-write 8-bit NV12M output;
G12/SM1 also support AM21C scatter capture. Keep compressed bodies alive
across display ownership and verify guards after decoder access ends.

Publish coded input endpoints separately from parser transport padding.
Restart the stream counter at a completed-picture boundary with saved
headers and reinitialize the workspace without returning an incomplete
picture.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5 Claude:claude-fable-5.1 Codex:gpt-5.6 Codex:gpt-6.0
[chewitt: reset the HEVC sub-engines on GX when the stream restarts,
 and drop the EXT_SPS_LT_RPS try_ctrl check that rejected the
 control's own initial value, and allocate the workspace and MV
 buffers per session on G12/SM1 as on GX instead of caching them
 across sessions, which held ~30 MB of CMA while idle]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
